\n```python\r\ndef test():\r\n   l = []\r\n   for thing in l:\r\n      x = lambda: print( thing )\r\n      x()\r\n\r\n   for thing in l:\r\n      print( thing )\r\n```\r\n  \r\nIf I initialize the list, l, to anything besides the empty list, then the W0631 warning goes away.  Or instead if I delete the second for-loop, the W0631 warning goes away as well.\r\n    \r\nSeems similar to this bug: https://github.com/PyCQA/pylint/issues/202\r\n\r\n### Configuration\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Command used\r\n\r\n```shell\r\npylint test.py\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Pylint output\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n% pylint test.py\r\n************* Module test\r\ntest.py:16:25: W0640: Cell variable thing defined in loop (cell-var-from-loop)\r\ntest.py:16:25: W0631: Using possibly undefined loop variable 'thing' (undefined-loop-variable)\r\n\r\n-----------------------------------\r\nYour code has been rated at 8.46/10\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nI don't expect to see W0631 (undefined-loop-variable).  The (cell-var-from-loop) warning is warranted.\r\n\r\n### Pylint version\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n% pylint --version\r\npylint 2.11.1\r\nastroid 2.8.5\r\nPython 3.8.12 (default, Aug 31 2021, 12:46:19)\r\n[GCC 8.4.0 20200304 (Red Hat 8.4.0-4)]\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### OS / Environment\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Additional dependencies\r\n\r\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/6419/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/6419/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]